  "releaseNotes": "v0.6.0 (2026-03-14):\n\n            ADDED:\n            - Raw buffer mode for zero-copy sample delivery via Channel<RawSampleBuffer>\n            - RawSampleBuffer type wrapping pooled byte[] buffers from ArrayPool<byte>\n            - UseRawBufferMode property to opt-in to raw buffer mode (default: false)\n            - GetRawSamplesFromAsyncBuffer() method returning RawSampleBuffer?\n            - Demo5: Raw buffer mode sample application\n\n            PERFORMANCE:\n            - Raw buffer mode eliminates per-sample IQData object allocation in async callback\n            - Single memcpy per callback replaces per-sample struct construction and queue operations\n            - ArrayPool<byte> reuse eliminates steady-state heap allocation in native callback path\n            - Channel<RawSampleBuffer> with SingleWriter/SingleReader for lock-free buffer handoff\n\n            See CHANGELOG.md for complete details.",
